rs on \"how to talk about the cost of study abroad,\" and educating students on the long-term investment in study abroad.\nOn-going activities for University of Minnesota faculty, staff, and academic advisers on curriculum integration include these engagement opportunities.\nLearning Abroad Center professionals continue to work with departments to internationalize undergraduate curricula with study abroad.\nCan you summarize the University of Minnesota's vision to internationalize the undergraduate experience and how they are encouraging study abroad?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nThe University of Minnesota aims to internationalize the undergraduate experience by integrating study abroad into the curriculum. They encourage faculty and academic advisers to review learning outcomes and develop a Study Abroad Major Advising Sheet to improve communication with students. The initiative addresses the financial concern of students through scholarship development and education on the long-term investment in study abroad. The university continues to work with departments to internationalize undergraduate curricula with study abroad.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nCan you provide more information on the Assess, Match, Motivate method of integrating study abroad into the undergraduate curricula at the University of Minnesota?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nCertainly! The Assess, Match, Motivate method of integrating study abroad into the undergraduate curricula at the University of Minnesota involves several steps:\n\n1. Assess: Faculty and academic advisers review the le","tokens":["<","|","im","_","start","|>","system","\n","You"," are"," a"," helpful"," assistant",".<","|","im","_","end","|>","\n","<","|","im","_","start","|>","user","\n","University"," of"," Minnesota"," leadership"," set"," a"," vision"," to"," international","ize"," the"," undergraduate"," experience",","," a"," vision"," that"," involves"," all"," campuses",","," colleges",","," and"," academic","